{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -la /home/rafa/Documents/zmoot; find /home/rafa/Documents/zmoot -name AGENTS.md -o -name CLAUDE.md; rg -n -i 'corgi|maximum variable|variable.*fee' /home/rafa/Documents/zmoot --glob '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"total 48\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   220 Nov  5 21:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa    26 Oct 20 22:40 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   108 Aug 22 12:56 .claude\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   188 Nov  6 08:13 .git\n-rw-r--r-- 1 rafa rafa   276 Aug 22 12:57 .gitignore\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   200 Nov  5 21:37 .obsidian\n-rw-r--r-- 1 rafa rafa  2028 Oct  5 21:01 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 rafa rafa 30151 Nov  6 21:15 CLAUDE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 rafa rafa   108 Aug 25 14:11 Cargan.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 rafa rafa     5 Aug  1 19:43 Chase card.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa    98 Nov  5 22:29 Home\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   140 Nov  5 21:37 Rafa\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   676 Nov  6 07:59 Reference\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   862 Nov  6 08:09 Shared\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   620 Oct 11 11:26 raka\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   186 Nov  5 21:37 z2027\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 rafa rafa   496 Oct 11 11:43 zArchive\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/AGENTS.md\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/AGENTS.md\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/CLAUDE.md\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/00 Inbox/ETF inbox.md:27:- **What is typically the maximum variable fee that can be charged on ETF redemptions?** No source supports a typical maximum, and none was inferred from unrelated redemption-fee rules.\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/10 Agent Work/reviews/ETF Participants.md.review.md:58:  - Corrects the note on AP agreements. In the ESS and ActiveShares forms, the distributor and the AP sign, the transfer agent accepts, and the trust is only a third-party beneficiary. Some newer trusts do sign (Corgi ETF Trust I, 2025).\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Market Mechanics.md:45:US ('40 Act), ETF: the AP pays the fund's creation and redemption fees unless waived or paid by another party. These cover the fund's processing and trading costs, protecting remaining shareholders from dilution. Fixed charges may go to the custodian; variable charges go to the fund. An AP may charge its own clients a fee or spread for handling creations and redemptions on their behalf.\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Market Mechanics.md:47:- **Transaction fees — US ('40 Act), ETF:** “I believe” the typical maximum variable creation/redemption fee is 3% (Rafael, 2026-11-06 (practitioner knowledge; may not be public)). Corgi's filed SAI specifies “up to 3%”; that is a filing example, not a universal cap. [Corgi ETF Trust I SAI, “Creation Transaction Fees” / “Redemption Transaction Fees”](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2078265/000182912625010217/corgietftrusti_n-1aa.htm).\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Market Mechanics.md:57:- Rafael, 2026-11-06 (practitioner knowledge; may not be public): cash settlement of derivatives and the anecdotal swap workaround; “I believe” a typical maximum variable fee of 3%.\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Market Mechanics.md:58:- Corgi ETF Trust I, filed SAI (2025-12-22), variable creation/redemption fees up to 3%, fixed fees to the custodian and variable fees to the fund: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2078265/000182912625010217/corgietftrusti_n-1aa.htm\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Market Mechanics.md:63:- Davis SAI supplement (2024-07-01), fixed processing fees and variable cash fees: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1670310/000007170124000048/497.htm\n/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/20 Knowledge/Finance/ETF/ETF Participants.md:646:  - AP agreement form signed by the trust: Corgi ETF Trust I (2025) https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2078265/000207826525000006/ex99e2_ap_form.htm\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
